   "new": "The interest rate the credit union was offering on new-vehicle loans as of 2026-06-30, as reported on NCUA Form 5300 Schedule A Section 1 line 5 (account 523). The instructions say to report rates 'being offered as of the reporting period' and, if more than one rate applies, 'the most common rate' in the category. Reported only by credit unions with new-vehicle loans outstanding. One rate per credit union: not tied to a credit score or term, and not an average of loans made. Label it 'a rate this credit union offers', never 'your rate'.",
   "used": "The interest rate the credit union was offering on used-vehicle loans as of 2026-06-30, as reported on NCUA Form 5300 Schedule A Section 1 line 6 (account 524). The instructions say to report rates 'being offered as of the reporting period' and, if more than one rate applies, 'the most common rate' in the category. Reported only by credit unions with used-vehicle loans outstanding. One rate per credit union: not tied to a credit score or term, and not an average of loans made. Label it 'a rate this credit union offers', never 'your rate'.",
   "stats": "n = credit unions kept; p25, median, p75 in percent (pandas linear interpolation), one value per credit union, unweighted. State = the credit union's mailing-address state in FOICU.txt, not where its members live. Small n (under about 10) gives unstable percentiles.",
   "outlier_rule": "Dropped rates more than 3 interquartile ranges outside the national 25th-75th percentile for that product; fences_pct shows the kept range."
